 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** See [Change Delivery Mechanism](../decisions/change-delivery-mechanism.md). Fast updates without realtime vendor bills or coupling. Polling was rejected for higher latency and repeated reads; hosted realtime services were rejected to avoid recurring fees and provider lock-in. Accepts connection management and reconnect complexity.
